# Mission Execution Protocol (Mission 29+)

After implementing a mission, auto-commit and push **only if ALL** conditions are true:

1. Tests passed
2. `next build` passed
3. Forbidden files untouched (`exchange.ts`, `contracts.ts`, router, wallet, swap, farms, pools, MasterChef, NFT, token lists)
4. No unrelated files changed
5. Working tree contains only mission-scoped files
6. No blockchain writes added
7. No router/contracts/wallet/swap/farms/pools/NFT logic modified
8. Mission output includes required manifest, if specified
9. Branch name is mission-specific (`missionXX-<short-kebab-title>`)
10. No merge and no PR created

## When all conditions pass — do automatically (no manual approval wait)

1. Create or switch to the dedicated mission branch
2. Commit **only** mission-scoped files
3. Push to origin
4. Return final report

**Commit message:** `Mission XX: <Mission Title>`

## Final report must include

- branch
- commit hash
- push status
- files committed
- tests/build result
- forbidden files untouched confirmation
- remaining uncommitted files
- Vercel status if available

## If ANY condition fails

- Do **not** commit
- Do **not** push
- Return the blocker and wait for instruction
